.TH OPEN_TEMP 3
.SH NAME
open_temp \- create and open a temporary file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "open.h"
.PP
.B int open_temp(char** pt);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B open_temp
creates and opens a temporary file based on a template. 
If 
.I pt
is non-null and points to a string, that string is used as the template.
Otherwise, it uses the default template "temp-XXXXXX.txt".
The 'XXXXXX' sequence is replaced by a random string to ensure the file name is unique.
.PP
The file is created with 
.B O_RDWR | O_CREAT | O_TRUNC | O_BINARY
flags.
.PP
On success, it returns a file descriptor to the opened file and updates 
.I *pt
with the name of the file created. The caller is responsible for deleting the file when it is no longer needed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a file descriptor on success, or -1 on error with 
.I errno
set appropriately.